&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Pretty comprehensive, isn&amp;rsquo;t it? So as you may have noticed, the problem is the interaction between Julia and Python. Note that &lt;code&gt;PyPlot&lt;/code&gt; depends on &lt;a href="https://github.com/JuliaPy/PyCall.jl"&gt;&lt;code&gt;PyCall&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (a package designed to call Python functions from Julia) and PyPlot actually depends on Python package &lt;a href="https://github.com/matplotlib/matplotlib"&gt;&lt;code&gt;matplotlib&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>